{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116462",
      "title": "Resolving Route-related Dynamic Data",
      "lectureOrder": 291,
      "videoOrder": 278,
      "sourceHash": "ed57794291ff7b43bdebc123600b59c13c24c69d504d12930c9375d0668c3b28",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.9,
          "end": 3,
          "en": "So what if you don't have static data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3,
          "end": 5.88,
          "en": "but dynamic data, as it's the case here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.88,
          "end": 10.05,
          "en": "where the data we fetch depends on a route parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.05,
          "end": 13.92,
          "en": "Well, the Angular router also helps you with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.92,
          "end": 17.61,
          "en": "though not with help of the data property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.61,
          "end": 20.19,
          "en": "Instead, you can add another property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.19,
          "end": 21.93,
          "en": "to your route configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.93,
          "end": 25.86,
          "en": "and that would be the resolve property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.86,
          "end": 29.55,
          "en": "And resolve now works a bit like data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.55,
          "end": 33.18,
          "en": "but for dynamic instead of static data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.18,
          "end": 35.79,
          "en": "because resolve wants an object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.79,
          "end": 38.37,
          "en": "where you can have key value pairs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.37,
          "end": 40.86,
          "en": "where the keys are totally up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.86,
          "end": 44.79,
          "en": "But the values then are not static data like they are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.79,
          "end": 46.23,
          "en": "in this data object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.23,
          "end": 51.15,
          "en": "But instead the values now must be valid angular resolvers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.15,
          "end": 55.08,
          "en": "which in modern Angular are simply functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.08,
          "end": 59.16,
          "en": "In older versions of Angular, you would use classes instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.16,
          "end": 62.1,
          "en": "and the next lecture will take care about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.1,
          "end": 65.193,
          "en": "Here we'll focus on the more modern style.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.12,
          "end": 68.85,
          "en": "Therefore, for example here, we could go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.85,
          "end": 72.18,
          "en": "to this user tasks component file here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.18,
          "end": 75.24,
          "en": "and add such a resolver function there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.24,
          "end": 77.7,
          "en": "though you could add it in any file you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.7,
          "end": 80.19,
          "en": "It doesn't have to be done there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.19,
          "end": 83.43,
          "en": "Therefore, what we could do is we could go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.43,
          "end": 87.15,
          "en": "to this user tasks component, TypeScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.15,
          "end": 91.41,
          "en": "and then there outside of that class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.41,
          "end": 94.44,
          "en": "we could export a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.44,
          "end": 97.12700000000001,
          "en": "that could be named resolveUserName,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.13,
          "end": 99.753,
          "en": "though the name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.71000000000001,
          "end": 101.88,
          "en": "I'm naming it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.88,
          "end": 105.57,
          "en": "because I plan on using it as a resolver function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.57,
          "end": 108.47999999999999,
          "en": "for this component, for this route here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.47999999999999,
          "end": 111.66,
          "en": "And because I plan to fetch the username,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.66,
          "end": 112.86,
          "en": "because that's also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.86,
          "end": 115.443,
          "en": "what we're doing here in ngOnInit it at the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.7,
          "end": 120.78,
          "en": "So therefore here we can define this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.78,
          "end": 125.13,
          "en": "and this function should then be a function that is accepted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.13,
          "end": 128.79,
          "en": "by Angular in that resolve array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.79,
          "end": 133.08,
          "en": "Now, to be accepted there, it must have a certain signature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.08,
          "end": 136.82999999999998,
          "en": "And to ensure this signature, I'll actually convert it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.82999999999998,
          "end": 140.46,
          "en": "to a function that's created slightly different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.46,
          "end": 143.28,
          "en": "by actually creating a constant or variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 143.28,
          "end": 146.61,
          "en": "named resolveUserName in which I then store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.61,
          "end": 149.19,
          "en": "a function like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.19,
          "end": 152.25,
          "en": "You can do that in JavaScript and TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.25,
          "end": 156.15,
          "en": "but this notation now allows me to assign a type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.15,
          "end": 159.15,
          "en": "to that constant, which then allows me to ensure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 159.15,
          "end": 162.167,
          "en": "that I set up the correct function signature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 162.167,
          "end": 166.32999999999998,
          "en": "because the type of this function should be resolveFn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 168.03,
          "end": 170.16,
          "en": "for resolve function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.16,
          "end": 174.663,
          "en": "And that is a type that is imported from @angular/router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 177,
          "end": 180.06,
          "en": "Now with that imported and assigned here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 180.06,
          "end": 182.07,
          "en": "we have to set up this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 182.07,
          "end": 185.79,
          "en": "such that it adheres to this type definition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 185.79,
          "end": 190.79,
          "en": "and it does adhere to that if it accepts two parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 190.92,
          "end": 194.46,
          "en": "where the first one is the activated route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 194.46,
          "end": 197.46,
          "en": "which is of type ActivatedRouteSnapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 200.76,
          "end": 202.44,
          "en": "So that's of course similar",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 202.44,
          "end": 206.52,
          "en": "to the activated route we injected earlier in this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 206.52,
          "end": 210.75,
          "en": "but now it's just that snapshot, which I already mentioned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 210.75,
          "end": 214.71,
          "en": "So that snapshot where you can't subscribe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 214.71,
          "end": 216.78,
          "en": "to parameters and so on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 216.78,
          "end": 219.66,
          "en": "because this resolver will be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 219.66,
          "end": 222.42000000000002,
          "en": "for every navigation action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 222.42000000000002,
          "end": 225.21,
          "en": "So every time this route gets active,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 225.21,
          "end": 227.64,
          "en": "this resolver function will be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 227.64,
          "end": 230.57999999999998,
          "en": "and it will then receive the latest snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 230.57999999999998,
          "end": 233.57999999999998,
          "en": "that describes this activated route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 233.57999999999998,
          "end": 236.55,
          "en": "That's why there is no reason to subscribe to it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 236.55,
          "end": 239.04,
          "en": "because it will be re executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 239.04,
          "end": 242.01,
          "en": "This function will be re executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 242.01,
          "end": 244.14,
          "en": "whenever the route becomes active,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 244.14,
          "end": 246.15,
          "en": "even if it already was active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 246.15,
          "end": 249.33,
          "en": "So it will be called again if the route parameter changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 249.33,
          "end": 250.383,
          "en": "for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 251.85,
          "end": 253.44,
          "en": "The second parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 253.44,
          "end": 257.853,
          "en": "that should be accepted here is the current router state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 258.756,
          "end": 261.213,
          "en": "which is of type RouterStateSnapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 263.07,
          "end": 265.412,
          "en": "So that's another type which just like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 265.412,
          "end": 270.412,
          "en": "ActivatedRouteSnapshot must be imported from Angular router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 273.45,
          "end": 277.23,
          "en": "Now in this resolver function, we then also need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 277.23,
          "end": 278.97,
          "en": "to return something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 278.97,
          "end": 282.3,
          "en": "We need to return the data that should be resolved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 282.3,
          "end": 284.88,
          "en": "by that function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 284.88,
          "end": 287.28,
          "en": "and that of course should be the username,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 287.28,
          "end": 290.97,
          "en": "which should be fetched basically as we're doing it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 290.97,
          "end": 293.283,
          "en": "with help of the user's service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 294.18,
          "end": 298.14,
          "en": "But this service is injected into this class here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 298.14,
          "end": 300.63,
          "en": "This resolver function here, however,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 300.63,
          "end": 302.4,
          "en": "is outside of this class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 302.4,
          "end": 305.01,
          "en": "It's not a class method and therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 305.01,
          "end": 307.893,
          "en": "it doesn't have access to that service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 309.18,
          "end": 314.18,
          "en": "But thankfully Angular allows you to inject things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 314.43,
          "end": 318.7,
          "en": "like services into these resolver functions as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 319.56,
          "end": 322.08299999999997,
          "en": "with help of this inject function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 322.95,
          "end": 324.81,
          "en": "Not with help of the constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 324.81,
          "end": 327.72,
          "en": "because functions don't have constructors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 327.72,
          "end": 330.45,
          "en": "but we can call the inject function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 330.45,
          "end": 332.79,
          "en": "in that resolver function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 332.79,
          "end": 336.42,
          "en": "and inject the UsersService.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 336.42,
          "end": 339.183,
          "en": "Angular will make sure that this works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 340.5,
          "end": 343.519,
          "en": "So that gives us access to that UsersService",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 343.519,
          "end": 346.32,
          "en": "in this resolver function as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 346.32,
          "end": 349.35,
          "en": "And with that injected, we can then get hold of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 349.35,
          "end": 351.03,
          "en": "that user name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 351.03,
          "end": 355.09000000000003,
          "en": "by basically executing the same code we have up here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 356.19,
          "end": 359.973,
          "en": "without this keyword since we're not in a class now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 361.5,
          "end": 366.21,
          "en": "But now we can call UsersService.users.find,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 366.21,
          "end": 369.303,
          "en": "but we also need to get access to the route parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 370.38,
          "end": 373.47,
          "en": "But we thankfully do get access to that with help of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 373.47,
          "end": 375.843,
          "en": "that ActivatedRouteSnapshot here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 377.19,
          "end": 380.28,
          "en": "So we can use our activatedRoute here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 380.28,
          "end": 383.1,
          "en": "because that has a paramMap property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 383.1,
          "end": 384.753,
          "en": "which has that get method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 385.95,
          "end": 387.87,
          "en": "So that's how we can get hold of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 387.87,
          "end": 389.49,
          "en": "And as I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 389.49,
          "end": 392.73,
          "en": "this resolver function will be re executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 392.73,
          "end": 395.28,
          "en": "every time the route parameter changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 395.28,
          "end": 398.58,
          "en": "So therefore we don't have to set up a subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 398.58,
          "end": 400.14,
          "en": "or anything like that here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 400.14,
          "end": 404.1,
          "en": "Instead it will be re executed automatically by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 404.1,
          "end": 406.413,
          "en": "whenever we load a different user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 407.82,
          "end": 410.67,
          "en": "And with that, we therefore then got the username",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 410.67,
          "end": 414.273,
          "en": "and we can return that here in that resolver function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 415.92,
          "end": 418.59000000000003,
          "en": "Now, TypeScript is still complaining here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 418.59000000000003,
          "end": 421.316,
          "en": "because actually it wants some extra information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 421.316,
          "end": 425.94,
          "en": "on that resolveFn type regarding the return value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 425.94,
          "end": 427.2,
          "en": "of this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 427.2,
          "end": 429.66,
          "en": "So you should add angle brackets here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 429.66,
          "end": 431.61,
          "en": "and then define the shape",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 431.61,
          "end": 433.98,
          "en": "of the data you are returning here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 433.98,
          "end": 436.743,
          "en": "And in my case, it's a simple string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 437.7,
          "end": 440.76,
          "en": "So between these angle brackets, in this case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 440.76,
          "end": 442.78,
          "en": "you should simply put string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 444.9,
          "end": 448.59,
          "en": "and that's then the finished resolver function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 448.59,
          "end": 452.64,
          "en": "The question now just is how you make that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 452.64,
          "end": 455.94,
          "en": "that's fetched by this function available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 455.94,
          "end": 460.53,
          "en": "to this component class here and to the overall component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 460.53,
          "end": 464.61,
          "en": "therefore, and the answer is essentially just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 464.61,
          "end": 468.483,
          "en": "as it was the case here with that static data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 469.44,
          "end": 473.55,
          "en": "If you have this ComponentInputBinding enabled,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 473.55,
          "end": 476.7,
          "en": "your resolved data will be made available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 476.7,
          "end": 481.47,
          "en": "to that target component as an input property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 481.47,
          "end": 486.18,
          "en": "So therefore what we should do is go to our route definition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 486.18,
          "end": 488.37,
          "en": "and then here in this resolve object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 488.37,
          "end": 492.513,
          "en": "you can pick any key name of your choice like username.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 494.25,
          "end": 499.25,
          "en": "As a value, you now should point at this resolver function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 499.62,
          "end": 502.44,
          "en": "so not at some static data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 502.44,
          "end": 505.023,
          "en": "Therefore the value here is resolveUserName.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 505.98,
          "end": 510.12,
          "en": "And this now should not be executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 510.12,
          "end": 512.34,
          "en": "You don't have parentheses here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 512.34,
          "end": 515.28,
          "en": "Instead you just point at this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 515.28,
          "end": 518.403,
          "en": "because Angular will execute it for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 519.45,
          "end": 522.78,
          "en": "And the value returned by that resolver function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 522.78,
          "end": 524.4,
          "en": "will then be made available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 524.4,
          "end": 528.27,
          "en": "to this component through an input with this name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 528.27,
          "end": 530.793,
          "en": "So in my case with the name userName.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 532.65,
          "end": 536.58,
          "en": "Therefore what we can and should do as a next and final step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 536.58,
          "end": 540.45,
          "en": "is go back to that user tasks component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 540.45,
          "end": 543.09,
          "en": "And there we can get rid of ngOnInit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 543.09,
          "end": 546.69,
          "en": "because that entire data fetching now no longer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 546.69,
          "end": 548.943,
          "en": "has to be performed in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 550.5,
          "end": 554.22,
          "en": "Instead we can now simply accept an input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 554.22,
          "end": 558.66,
          "en": "and we can get rid of all this code here as well, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 558.66,
          "end": 563.66,
          "en": "all of this and just change our username here, this property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 564.9,
          "end": 569.76,
          "en": "to be an input for example, by using the input function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 569.76,
          "end": 572.31,
          "en": "or by using the input decorator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 572.31,
          "end": 574.173,
          "en": "that of course would also work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 575.04,
          "end": 577.08,
          "en": "and it can be a required input here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 577.08,
          "end": 580.77,
          "en": "And I know that I'll get a value of type string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 580.77,
          "end": 582.813,
          "en": "So that's how we could set this up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 585.06,
          "end": 589.2,
          "en": "And this implements OnInit thing here also should go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 589.2,
          "end": 592.8,
          "en": "and we can and should it then all remove these unused",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 592.8,
          "end": 595.443,
          "en": "imports like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 598.38,
          "end": 601.89,
          "en": "And with that we got a much leaner component now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 601.89,
          "end": 605.82,
          "en": "It barely contains any code as you can tell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 179,
          "start": 605.82,
          "end": 609.24,
          "en": "Instead that's not all in that resolver function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 180,
          "start": 609.24,
          "end": 612.33,
          "en": "And that function could theoretically also be stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 181,
          "start": 612.33,
          "end": 614.28,
          "en": "in some other file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 182,
          "start": 614.28,
          "end": 616.2,
          "en": "and therefore we outsourced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 183,
          "start": 616.2,
          "end": 620.82,
          "en": "that data fetching task from the component to the resolver,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 184,
          "start": 620.82,
          "end": 622.62,
          "en": "which can be an elegant way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 185,
          "start": 622.62,
          "end": 626.253,
          "en": "of getting your component data when using routing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 186,
          "start": 627.24,
          "end": 629.88,
          "en": "Now since I'm using the input function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 187,
          "start": 629.88,
          "end": 631.95,
          "en": "username will be a signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 188,
          "start": 631.95,
          "end": 636.36,
          "en": "and therefore we should call it as such in our template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 189,
          "start": 636.36,
          "end": 638.613,
          "en": "to get that signal value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 190,
          "start": 640.35,
          "end": 644.01,
          "en": "But with that done, if you save everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 191,
          "start": 644.01,
          "end": 646.02,
          "en": "you should be able to go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 192,
          "start": 646.02,
          "end": 649.2,
          "en": "and still see that username here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 193,
          "start": 649.2,
          "end": 652.71,
          "en": "And you see it changes as you switch between users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 194,
          "start": 652.71,
          "end": 655.95,
          "en": "but now it's loaded with help of that resolver.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 195,
          "start": 655.95,
          "end": 659.19,
          "en": "And that's of course not a feature you have to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 196,
          "start": 659.19,
          "end": 662.88,
          "en": "because as you saw it worked without that as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 197,
          "start": 662.88,
          "end": 667.56,
          "en": "But it is a feature you can use to have leaner components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 198,
          "start": 667.56,
          "end": 670.89,
          "en": "That's in the end the main advantage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 199,
          "start": 670.89,
          "end": 675.03,
          "en": "And you could of course also have multiple resolvers here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 200,
          "start": 675.03,
          "end": 678.84,
          "en": "if you had multiple key value pairs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 201,
          "start": 678.84,
          "end": 680.613,
          "en": "that would all work.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
